### auth_lab.http — Authentication Gauntlet Lab
### Write your REST Client request blocks under each phase header.
### Run a block with Ctrl+Alt+R (Windows/Linux) or Cmd+Alt+R (macOS).
### Hint: all endpoints live under http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### PHASE 1 — Basic Authentication
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/basic/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Basic admin admin123

# TODO: Find the Basic Auth endpoint in api/urls.py.
# TODO: Write a GET request that sends credentials using the
#       Authorization: Basic <base64(username:password)> header.
#       Tip: REST Client supports  Authorization: Basic admin admin123  directly.


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### PHASE 3 — Token Authentication (Opaque)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/token/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Token 158f2939517814e070d1d9a8ba01b17ffc5cdd25

# TODO: Generate a DRF token for the admin user first (see lab README).
# TODO: Find the Token Auth endpoint in api/urls.py.
# TODO: Write a GET request that sends the token using the
#       Authorization: Token <your-token> header.

### Phase 3 — Tampered Token

GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/token/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Token 158f2939517814e070d1d9a8ba01b17ffc5cdd20

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### PHASE 4 — JSON Web Tokens (JWT)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/jwt/login/ HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "admin",
    "password": "admin123"
}

# TODO: Find the JWT login endpoint in api/urls.py.
# TODO: Write a POST request with a JSON body containing username and password.
# After sending, copy the "access" value from the response and paste it below:
#   @accessToken = <paste the access token here>
# TODO: Write a GET request to the protected JWT endpoint using:
#       Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
# TODO: (Bonus) Write a POST request to refresh the access token using
#       the refresh token from the login response.

### Phase 4 — JWT Protected Request
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/jwt/protected/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJ0b2tlbl90eXBlIjoiYWNjZXNzIiwiZXhwIjoxNzkwMTg3NTM5LCJpYXQiOjE3OTAxODU3MzksImp0aSI6IjNhNDE0MDk4NjU0YTRhZGM4YzFhODA1MzdmNmNlMjE3IiwidXNlcl9pZCI6IjEifQ.TOaiFa1fDXpOScICqwPp1V8FnZZyP4_dPeta3NaDCL8

